    pipes: [
        // ==== THE STATION SIDE ====================================
        // The supply main leaves the department at (18, 21), crosses the
        // south corridor on layer 4, and stops at the adapter -- three
        // tiles of blue that a technician can see, stand on and cut,
        // which is the whole reason the fittings are out here rather
        // than behind a bulkhead.
        (18, 20, 8), (19, 20, 8), (21, 20, 8),
        // ...and on the far side of the adapter, THE DISTRIBUTION RUN,
        // layer 3: a full ring under the Concourse with a spur into
        // every room the crew stands in. It is one net, so a vent in the
        // Workshop and a vent in the Cargo Hall are drawing on the same
        // body of gas as the department's own supply main -- which is
        // what a station main is, and what the first draft's twenty
        // tiles of pipe between two rooms could not demonstrate.
        (23, 20, 4), (23, 19, 4), (23, 18, 4), (22, 18, 4), (21, 18, 4),
        (20, 18, 4), (19, 18, 4), (18, 18, 4), (17, 18, 4), (16, 18, 4),
        (15, 18, 4), (14, 18, 4), (13, 18, 4), (12, 18, 4), (11, 18, 4),
